<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Radviliškis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1919</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuanian-wars-of-independence">Lithuanian Wars of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Radviliškis was fought in November 1919 around the railway town of Radviliškis in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, where Lithuanian forces defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-russian-volunteer-army">West Russian Volunteer Army</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pavel-bermondt-avalov">Pavel Bermondt-Avalov</a>. The victory, on 21–22 November, forced the Bermontians to withdraw from Lithuania under Allied supervision by mid-December. It was the decisive engagement of Lithuania's brief war against the Bermontians.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-radviliskis.jpg" alt="Battle of Radviliškis" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Emilis Jeneris · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Radvili%C5%A1kis_painting,_c._1920,_Emilis_Jeneris.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
